  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "The current best configuration is config_015 (scvi_n200, vit_l, avgpool, concat) at 0.7150 acc / 0.6872 F1. With scgpt, transformer aggregation was clearly worse than avgpool (0.520 vs 0.542, config_023 vs config_007), but scvi_n200 produces qualitatively richer and higher-performing representations, so the aggregation–encoder interaction may differ. Config_011 changes only the aggregation (avgpool → transformer) while holding the best-known RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion method constant, giving a clean single-variable test. If transformer underperforms, we confirm avgpool is optimal and can pivot to testing profile setting or image encoder; if it improves, we gain a direct performance boost on the best pipeline. This is the most informative next step because it isolates one architectural decision on the strongest configuration identified so far, maximizing information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

